    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0122" n="38" xml:id="pg38"/>

                <head>No. 8.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName corresp="#p_DEC1" type="from"
                            >Clapp</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_WH1" type="to"
                            >Hunter</persName></hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United
                                States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Buenos
                            Ayres</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1873-04-15"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April</hi> 15, 1873</date>. (Received May
                        21.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 34.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that General
                    Bartoloiné Mitre, having returned from his mission to Brazil, in which it
                    appears that he has been entirely successful in placing the delicate questions
                    between the two countries, arising out of the Paraguayan alliance, on a
                    satisfactory basis, has been dispatched to Paraguay, with full powers to
                    negotiate the treaty which the above-mentioned alliance contemplates.</p>
                <p>The Brazilian minister to this country, Baron <persName>de Magallaens</persName>,
                    has also gone to Paraguay to represent Brazilian interests.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_DEC1">DEXTER E. CLAPP</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
